<!--
  The adaptive-icon foreground: the Podsilo mark in white, on the accent background declared in
  `values/ic_launcher_background.xml`. Converted from `assets/logos/ic_launcher_foreground.xml`,
  which is the exported source (docs/logo.md §2/§3).

  Two bars falling into an open silo, one band already stored — a signal being caught and kept,
  which is the app's whole job. It avoids the two obvious clichés: a microphone, which this app is
  deliberately not about, and an RSS wave, which every feed reader already uses.

  GEOMETRY IS CONSTRAINED, NOT ARBITRARY. An adaptive icon is a 108x108 dp canvas of which launchers
  may mask anything outside the central 66 dp circle, and they crop to circles, squircles and
  rounded squares depending on the device. The group below scales the 100-unit mark by 0.60 (60 dp)
  and centres it, so the whole figure sits inside that circle with room to spare. Do not re-scale it
  at the call site — logo.md §3 says this file is already at the safe-zone size.

  The same drawable is the `monochrome` layer in `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml`: the launcher
  discards its colour and recolours the silhouette from the wallpaper palette, so the mark has to
  read on its gaps alone. It does — that is what the 10-unit stroke buys.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <group
        android:scaleX="0.60"
        android:scaleY="0.60"
        android:translateX="24"
        android:translateY="24">

        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:pathData="M30,6 h40 v10 h-40 z" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:pathData="M36,24 h28 v10 h-28 z" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#00000000"
            android:pathData="M18,42 V94 H82 V42"
            android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:strokeWidth="10" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:pathData="M32,70 h36 v10 h-36 z" />
    </group>
</vector>
